1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,480
Here are eight things that you can implement today to not just exit your lonely girl era but to also accept and transform your life quick.
她说，接下来有八件今天就能做的事，帮助自己走出所谓的孤独女孩阶段，接纳并改变生活。

2
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:14,270
You get to decide okay since I don't have many people around me podcasts books you get to control the five closest influences in your life.
独处时，你可以决定身边的影响来源，比如播客和书；她认为最亲近的五种影响也能自己选择。

3
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:21,360
And sometimes what friends don't even realize are weighing you down by just the things that they're saying how they're complaining about their own lives.
她觉得，一些朋友可能没有意识到，自己的话语和对生活的抱怨会让你感到负担。

4
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:28,520
And so in this time where you are by yourself in this time where you are a bit more secluded it's this time where you get to shape your entire world.
在独处、更少和外界接触的这段时间，她觉得人可以重新塑造自己的世界。

5
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:34,600
When you have that time to really sit down and stamp who you truly are you won't let nobody call you by the wrong name.
当你坐下来明确自己是谁时，她说，就不会容许别人给自己贴上错误标签。

6
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:40,310
Not let no one say girl do you be lazy uh uh I'm just a little tired today but don't be lazy I be on my stuff.
她举例说，别人说自己懒时，她会反驳：今天只是有点累，自己平时是有在认真做事的。

7
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,310
You see her hair though oh no girl you trying to be messy that's not my name messy not my name.
有人想拿别人的头发说闲话时，她会说：别把我带进这种是非里，那不是我想要的标签。

8
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:49,920
Get to really hone into who am I and what name do I want to be called by what do I want to be seen as.
她说，要认真想想：我是谁，想被怎样称呼，希望别人怎样看待自己。

9
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:55,630
The first thing that I started to do when I began to move out of my lonely girl era limit my doom scrolling.
她开始走出那个阶段时，首先做的事就是限制自己漫无目的地刷负面信息。

10
00:00:55,640 --> 00:01:02,840
When you are doom scrolling you're just seeing people's highlight reels best part of the day the best part of the function the best part of the event.
她说，刷屏时看到的往往是别人的精彩片段：一天、聚会或活动里最好的部分。

11
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:05,760
Might be dead as hell but they video recording that one little corner.
她认为，整个活动可能很冷清，但镜头只拍下一个热闹的小角落。

12
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:09,160
You wouldn't even know you're just in your bed feeling like you're missing out on life.
你可能完全不知道这些，只是在床上看着，觉得自己错过了生活。

13
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,830
You don't have to be around people to live your life if that's not the season you're in.
她说，过自己的生活并不一定要有人陪伴，尤其当你正处于一个需要独处的阶段。

14
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,150
That's not the life that you're supposed to be living at that moment.
在她看来，当下并不一定适合过那种总有人围绕的生活。

15
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:19,750
Doom scrolling could give you the misconception that people's lives are better than they really are.
她认为，刷屏可能让你误以为别人的生活比实际更好。

16
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:24,950
A night but they're not coming on camera the next morning with that lace half all with their hair hurting no one showing the.
她举夜晚过后第二天的样子作例子，说大家不会展示头发凌乱、不舒服的一面；这句字幕有缺损，待核验。

17
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,710
A long time I didn't either so I have no place to judge.
她说，自己很长时间也没展示这些，所以并没有资格去评判别人。

18
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:33,750
Showing they have no funds in the trip they're not showing the man that's really paying for the trip on a loan yes he got her that watch but he hits her.
她继续举例说，网上可能看不到旅行缺钱、别人借钱买单，甚至送表的人会施暴等背面；这是她举出的情境。

19
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:37,990
You have to be careful with that whole doom scrolling I really limit my doom scrolling to when I'm on the treadmill.
所以她会留意这种刷屏，把自己的刷屏时间限制在跑步机上。

20
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,160
Cuz even if I'm doom scrolling it's like okay but I'm getting buff out of it I really don't need to be doom scrolling but my butt is getting better as we scroll.
她开玩笑说，虽然还在刷屏，但至少同时在锻炼，臀部状态也在改善。

21
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:47,880
God give and take so it's like I know I'm not going to cut doom scrolling out of my life completely.
她打趣说有得也有失，并承认不会彻底从生活里戒掉刷屏。

22
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:53,520
But I set a specific time where I say I'm going to allow myself to doom scroll right here and right now.
她会规定具体时间，告诉自己，就在此时此地允许自己刷一会儿。

23
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:58,830
Once I leave this gym once I get off this treadmill once I get off this stair master I'm going to be back to regular program.
一旦离开健身房、跑步机或踏步机，她就要回到正常的生活安排。

24
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:01,430
Back to looking at my own life pouring into my own self.
也就是重新关注自己的生活，把精力投入自己身上。

25
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:04,760
You're using mental emotional and nervous system energy.
她认为，刷屏会消耗心理、情绪及神经系统的能量；这是作者的个人说法。

26
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,950
Think you're not using it cuz you're in the bed you're laying down you're eating snacks.
你可能觉得自己没在消耗什么，因为只是躺在床上吃零食。

27
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:11,629
You're actually draining your mind you're draining your emotional capacity.
但她觉得，这仍然会耗尽自己的心力和情绪承受空间。

28
00:02:11,639 --> 00:02:16,510
Assign your doom scroll time to somewhere not when you're just in the bed feeling depressed feeling bad for yourself.
她建议把刷屏安排在特定场合，而不是躺在床上感到低落、自怜的时候；这里不是医学判断。

29
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,080
And the second thing that I did was change the narrative.
她做的第二件事，是改变自己的叙事方式。

30
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:24,520
I stopped saying that I was alone and I started saying I'm spending more time pouring into myself.
她不再说自己孤身一人，而是说自己正在花更多时间照顾和充实自己。

31
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:28,360
To delulu your way into a better life you got to delulu your way into a better mindset.
她用俚语 delulu 开玩笑，说先换一种积极想象生活的方式，也许心态会随之变化。

32
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:35,400
Have to take yourself out of that victim mindset or you'll never attract the high value friends and friendships and community that you deserve.
她认为，要走出自己所说的受害者心态，才更可能建立自己期待的友谊与社群；这是她的价值判断。

33
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:40,600
If you're a victim don't nobody want to be around no victim don't nobody want to be around nobody who feel bad for themselves all day.
她尖锐地说，人们不愿一直陪着整天自怜的人；这只是她的评价，不应概括受害者。

34
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:48,800
Just talk down about themselves about their appearance about their finances about their mentality nobody wants to be around that type of person that person sucks that person is annoying.
她继续批评总贬低自己外貌、财务或心理状态的人，称那样的人令人厌烦；保留其尖锐语气，不代表事实。

35
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,680
You have to change your narrative instead of saying I'm alone I'm lonely I have no friends.
她再次强调，要改变叙事，不再反复说自己孤单、没有朋友。

36
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:56,600
Start saying I'm choosing to spend this time getting to know myself better.
她建议换成：我选择花这段时间，更好地认识自己。

37
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,880
Get you some eye patches some candles take a bath.
她说，可以准备眼膜、蜡烛，泡个澡。

38
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:06,120
You don't want to miss valuable lessons because you was trying to speed through a space in your life that's supposed to be getting you ready for the next stage in your life.
她认为，不要急着跳过某个人生阶段，因为这段时间可能正在为下一阶段做准备，里面也有值得学的事。

39
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:09,120
Embrace it and turn bs into butterflies okay.
她让大家接纳这段经历，并用一句俏皮话说，要把糟糕经历变成蝴蝶般的变化。

40
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:15,840
After writing those two things down I stepped into solo hobbies I was drawing I was customizing purses I was painting scrapbooking.
写下前两点后，她开始尝试独自做的爱好，比如画画、改造手袋和做剪贴簿。

41
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,990
Started posting on tiktok more just making it a digital diary.
她也开始更常在 TikTok 发内容，把它当作数字日记。

42
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,440
Started going to the gym more I started doing things by myself.
她去健身房的次数更多，也开始自己做事情。

43
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:29,120
Sitting down with yourself and doing activity and taking your time and listening to music you will begin to fall in love with your alone time.
她觉得，独自坐下来做活动，慢慢来、听听音乐，会让人渐渐喜欢上独处时间。

44
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:32,230
And it will also help contribute to changing your narrative.
她认为，这也会帮助改变自己对独处的理解。

45
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:36,559
You're telling yourself oh I'm not alone I don't feel lonely I'm just in between friends right now.
她会告诉自己，不是孤单，而是暂时处于两段友谊之间。

46
00:03:36,559 --> 00:03:39,559
And when you actually start spending time with yourself and start enjoying it.
真正开始和自己相处，并享受其中。

47
00:03:39,559 --> 00:03:42,720
It will back up the things that you were saying to yourself.
她说，这会印证自己之前对自己说的话。

48
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,240
I was cooking I made a pot roast.
她还会做饭，甚至做过炖烤肉。

49
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:49,440
That is another opportunity for you to connect to a person on a deeper more creative level.
她觉得，这些爱好又能成为和别人建立更深入、更有创造力的联结的机会。

50
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:54,080
Now you're not just confined to the people who like to just drink or party or talk mess.
这样，朋友圈就不再只限于喜欢喝酒、聚会或说闲话的人。

51
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:57,040
Now you're starting to find friends oh you like to read oh me too.
你开始发现朋友也喜欢读书，于是可以说：我也是。

52
00:03:57,040 --> 00:04:00,000
Oh you like to take long walks and look at nature take some pictures oh me too.
或者发现彼此都喜欢散步、看大自然和拍照。

53
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,620
Oh you like to cook oh me too.
又或者，双方都喜欢做饭。
